      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: railroad crossings, city, rural and interstate driving",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: railroad crossings, city, rural and interstate driving\nAudience: first-time North Carolina applicants preparing for the regular Class C knowledge test, in English; the railroad stopping distances [A01] and light distances [A06] are exact-number recall items.\nLevel: legal rules quoted from statute plus procedure sequences for crossings and interstates; scenario drills fit the gate and stall situations.\nPrerequisites: the speed section (two-second rule, stopping distance) and the school bus section, since buses must stop at crossings.\nSensitivity: railroad emergency guidance is safety-critical and stated as printed, including get-out-first ordering.\n",
